{"title":"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e6cd0e4103015efba12e0fc4291f012b467eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of positive integers. A function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a5f7d3075af89ec1d3f6cbdada5588ca99d403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{N}\\to\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> satisfies the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e73ff2f75b103e9d6a4004a42e4ed7f4ee64a67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\underbrace{f(f(\\ldots f}_{f(n)\\text{ times}}(n)\\ldots))=\\frac{n^2}{f(f(n))}\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"57\" />for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Given this information, determine all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/23550dc2a45990001b48eb81fa95f1c54f758d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1000)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/247997d76df5770d47559bcdbd798dd478c5d8f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^r(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> denote the result when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is applied to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b2e2fcdef2fe304bafde2869b6098f72152395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{r-1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"19\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d876709128ff01eeb85ae96a29e7ead51afaea0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^1(x)=f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"19\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b41b2440b2af66aa29523fd7fb135b25d0ee6c0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hfill \\break \\hfill \\break$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"42\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52bb7a6bbb4b04541b1e8a0d9ff870e0f70bc8a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p)=f(q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/986a850a98d42a8fe326e758b6828720dbc7b3fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(p)=f^2(q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1df57e80eaab057054b389caf36ebf22a3e35d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{f(p)}(p)=f^{f(q)}(q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/8862d00ab10eb6194a6430aaab7b728744dd4825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies p^2=f^2(p)\\cdot f^{f(p)}(p)=f^2(q)\\cdot f^{f(q)}(q)=q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"377\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f98811f9bed5d7410959ffaa735d7d1225bb61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies p=\\pm q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/8/1b82d6cca441c61e1b3ad1a3d86720db64b74d5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies p=q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8fffb34b215ac3122a73f2d3b43017cbb80e6989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is injective. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21e723a6dd27b6826f89b025248fc5d80c44773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> is also injective.\n</p><p><br />\nLemma 1: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8200776c201dd41ad9656bf6478dc7ad748ce2f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^r(b)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65ca28262d1839811dfac35a4384e450abe507c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4d6c17fef7c3d0a099d86cb13c69c5ef21fc480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=a$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nProof:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee156bd9d4adef458c1923ca3b4c4a81b3f07d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^r(b)=a=f^r(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" /> which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4d6c17fef7c3d0a099d86cb13c69c5ef21fc480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=a$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> by injectivity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21e723a6dd27b6826f89b025248fc5d80c44773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nLemma 2: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5612db8088a0cbd39612e7b65284198f99a7b3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(m)=f^{f(m)}(m)=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92d9ae2bd203734ff276612634566238922b1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m)=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nProof:\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54a3b360822d516fb91a95e5e70d70418f7376bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbec2551c6dfd2f9d9a4c964a51db1b1a577a637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(m)=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530d3879f1e80f6c6b6551b6ea556fd577993dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89ffd003d5888bd3edbf29b729b694be1757d7ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(k)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fe91aef3dcbf63f6b1a62b0cad886b131576569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\newline f^2(k)\\cdot f^{f(k)}(k)=k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958fa26776f39b396f55c320bb2ccebb91c962b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\neq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/1549ee56c299bcb22c3a23e1beafce472ed78d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{f(k)}(k)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a656a15c3c10c956a27d8e3570d33a7c67c66e1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies f^m(k)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df5002a8e776c972e1f9ab5c7aeed20e0ab237ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies f^{gcd(m, 2)}(k)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96f6bde884668f2d8db248e0991309d305290db6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies f(k)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This proves Lemma 2.\n</p><p><br />\nI claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92d9ae2bd203734ff276612634566238922b1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m)=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> for all odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Otherwise, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the least counterexample.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/56340324456676ea225f73780dd8a2e663701c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(m)\\cdot f^{f(m)}(m)=m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />, either\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01ec430d2d9de6ffffd8b5e6bb1418feb1d88954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1) f^2(m)=k&lt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" />, contradicted by Lemma 1 since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89ffd003d5888bd3edbf29b729b694be1757d7ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(k)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92f9e6843ff1941dd2dfcfa54baa2bf6997a086.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2) f^{f(m)}(m)=k&lt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" />, also contradicted by Lemma 1 by similar logic.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/d/4ed25bda83b9338c68847a411d883095ed9dfa26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3) f^2(m)=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/addba4aa39f1aae4b576c2e13d9057cf86d25422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{f(m)}(m)=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"23\" />, which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92d9ae2bd203734ff276612634566238922b1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m)=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> by Lemma 2.\nThis proves the claim.\n</p><p><br />\nBy injectivity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/23550dc2a45990001b48eb81fa95f1c54f758d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1000)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> is not odd.\nI will prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/23550dc2a45990001b48eb81fa95f1c54f758d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1000)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> can be any even number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/263e6b5cc2ff7f9d83349a72ce219147365e8c43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1000)=x, f(x)=1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83ffe7f081bfaaca429cf1f3c1c33abf88744951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> for all other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d132a7700f53288a29cd601f271ec2fad55a8da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(n)\\cdot f^{f(n)}(n)=n\\cdot n=n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"20\" />. This satisfies the given property.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d132a7700f53288a29cd601f271ec2fad55a8da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(n)\\cdot f^{f(n)}(n)=n\\cdot n=n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f51cad099dcb53008782b43db56068e43a3e5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^2(n)=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"19\" />. This satisfies the given property.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO\" title=\"2019 USAMO\">2019 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2019\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\"><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018011502\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.075 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 369/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1262/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 55/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11778/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   22.784      1 -total\n 74.30%   16.929      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 24.93%    5.679      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17478:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018011502 and revision id 151066. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}